      "ground": "The argument erroneously cites Article 8(2)(b)(iv) for the crime of 'extensive destruction,' which is actually located at Article 8(2)(a)(iv) for international armed conflicts.",
      "reasoning": "Article 8(2)(b)(iv) of the Rome Statute prohibits intentionally launching attacks with knowledge that incidental civilian harm is excessive. It does not define the crime of 'extensive destruction of property not justified by military necessity.' That crime is enumerated in Article 8(2)(a)(iv), a grave breach. Misidentifying the specific treaty provision undermines the legal basis for the characterization of the conduct as that specific war crime.",
      "severity": "material",
